course: dictionary
lesson: 6082
title: Metallic: made of metal, or like metal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Metallic is an adjective. It describes something that is made of metal, or that has the qualities of metal. «Asteroids are rocky or metallic leftovers from the birth of the Solar System.» Some asteroids are rock and some are metal, so metallic means made of metal here.
explain: Metallic can also mean shiny like metal. «Metallic paint» and «metallic blue» are shiny colours, like silver or gold, not dull colours. The word tells you how the paint or colour looks.
explain: A metallic sound is hard and ringing, like a spoon hitting a pan. A metallic taste is like the taste of a coin. The words around the word give the clue: you can say what the sound or taste is like, and metallic is the word for it.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Asteroids are rocky or made of metal leftovers» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Metallic means made of metal, or looking, sounding or tasting like metal.
fact: «Metallic paint» is shiny, like gold, silver or steel.
fact: Most metals are shiny, hard and strong, and they conduct heat and electricity.
fact: Most metals are not magnetic. Iron, nickel and cobalt are the exceptions.
fact: A metallic sound is hard and ringing, and a metallic taste is like a coin.
exercise: «Asteroids are rocky or metallic leftovers from the birth of the Solar System.» What does metallic mean here? | *Made of metal | Very rocky and wet | Floating in water | Brand new and bright
exercise: «The car was painted metallic blue.» What does metallic suggest about the colour? | *Shiny, like metal | Soft and fluffy | Very old | Dull and grey
exercise: Ella bit a spoon and said, «It tastes metallic.» What does a metallic taste remind you of? | Like rain | Like strawberries | *Like a coin | Like warm bread
test: «The knight's armour gave a metallic clang as he fell.» What does metallic mean here? | Soft and quiet | *Hard and ringing, like metal hitting metal | Wet and muddy | Sweet and sticky
test: Which of these is a metallic material? | Sand | *Copper | Wood | Rubber
exam: Tom wants to check the meaning of metallic in «a metallic taste». Which is the best way? | Count the letters in the word | Read only the word aloud | Skip the sentence and ignore the clues | *Swap in a meaning, such as «like a coin», and see if the sentence still makes sense
